# rule.always.catch-dreams-for-followups

> **every followup you do not do becomes a caught dream — and the route that found it keeps a symlink to it.**

🟡 first run the SAFE/CLEAN test (`rule.always.fix-forward-under-scouts-honor`) — its PAIR, booted beside it here.

- a dream is the second-best outcome: safe and clean means fix it now, and no dream is owed
- ⇒ this rule governs what the large half owes
- ⇒ a role that holds this half alone inverts the default and reads the dream as the primary move
  - so the pair boots together, always: a role that carries one carries both

the shape and the four kinds are the `dream` contract — `term=artifact.dream._.choice._.md`.

## .why — a spoken followup is a deletion in a polite coat

| kept by a dream | why it matters |
|---|---|
| the cue that fired | *what made you notice* is what a later reader cannot reconstruct |
| the reason it was deferred | so the next traveler does not re-derive the judgment and defer again |
| the shape of the fix | you held the context. that comprehension is the expensive half |

## 🔴 .why the symlink

```sh
rhx symlink --at "$route/dreams/v$date.$kind.$slug.md" \
            --to ".dream/v$date.$kind.$slug.md" \
            --mode relative --idem findsert
```

🟡 a deferral for DIRT owes a FULCRUM too.

- the dream records the work; the fulcrum records the decision to defer it
- a dream alone reports the work and hides the call
- ⇒ and the ripple estimate that made it dirty is a best guess, which is what a fulcrum list exists to surface

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you would say *"i'll flag that for later"* | 🔴 that phrase IS the cue. run the two questions, then fix it or catch it |
| a rule you just wrote fires on your very next action and you route around it | 🔴 the sharpest cue. the rule found a real gap and you skipped it |
| you hit a broken paved path — a documented command that fails, a stale readme | catch it. a documented defect is worse than an absent doc |
| a fix belongs to another repo | catch it as a `reseed` dream. a tree adopts only what is scoped to itself |
| you cannot push a seed | 🔴 `.dream/` is the local queue. caught is not dispatched |
| a fix is large — a rename across files, a contract change, a migration | catch it, with the shape of the fix |
| you finish a route with an empty `$route/dreams/` | 🔴 suspicious. a real round finds at least one item it could not clean |

## .the shape

`# 🌙 dream: $what-is-owed` · kind · owner · caught $date, then: `.the cue that fired` · `.the gap, precisely` (with checkable evidence) · `.the shape of the fix` · `.why it is not done in this round` (the SAFE/CLEAN answer).

blocker: a followup mentioned and never caught · a dream caught for a fix that was safe and clean (that was a fix) · a dream with no symlink at the route that found it · a dream that lives inside a route rather than `.dream/` · a dirt deferral with no fulcrum. nitpick: no `.the shape of the fix`.
